From: Package maintainers <packages@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] layer the classid and packet-location databases
Source: downstream
Upstream: not submitted; suitable for upstream review

Read complete databases from the administrator, transient, and vendor paths.
Keep NLSYSCONFDIR as an exact override. When the library generates a class ID,
seed the administrator database from the selected lower file before appending
so the new whole-file override retains package entries.

Track the selected path as part of each reader cache, and correct the invalid
tree-destruction call that made a nonempty class-database reload abort.

diff --git a/Makefile.am b/Makefile.am
index 227fa56..daf1724 100644
--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -46,6 +46,8 @@ warn_cppflags = \
 
 defines_cppflags = \
 	-D_NL_SYSCONFDIR_LIBNL=\"$(sysconfdir)/libnl\" \
+	-D_NL_RUNTIMEDIR_LIBNL=\"/run/libnl\" \
+	-D_NL_VENDORDIR_LIBNL=\"$(prefix)/lib/libnl\" \
 	-D_NL_PKGLIBDIR=\"$(pkglibdir)\" \
 	$(NULL)
 
